r 594, 1269, 1460, 1701 add at most 1-2 idiosyncratic extras (step_21..24). Jaccard overlap of before/after contact sets at every candidate change point is therefore ~1, giving peak dissimilarity ~0.0-0.03 (step_29), far below the 0.6 threshold. The activity is a rotating relay over a static audience, not an abrupt partner turnover.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 74985, "total_output_tokens": 8731, "total_tokens": 83716, "total_latency_ms": 124477, "llm_calls": 12, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}